.TH MYSTRLEN 3 "November 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrlen \- calculate the length of a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <mystrfunctions.h>
.sp
.BI "size_t mystrlen(const char *" str );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrlen
function computes the length of the string pointed to by
.IR str ,
not including the terminating null byte.
It is a custom reimplementation of the standard library's
.BR strlen (3)
function, provided as part of the
.B libmyutils
educational library.
.PP
If
.I str
is
.B NULL
the function returns 0 rather than causing undefined behaviour.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters in
.IR str ,
excluding the null terminator.
Returns 0 if
.I str
is
.BR NULL .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <mystrfunctions.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("%zu\en", mystrlen("hello"));  /* prints 5 */
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Written as part of the OS Assignment 01: Core C Utilities Library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR strlen (3)
